        "original_id": "233665f6-ae09-5605-b844-26f7a4b3c493",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jaroslav Kvapil\n- Places: Chudenice, Prague, Kingdom of Bohemia, Central Europe\n- Roles: poet, playwright, librettist\n- Concepts: Czech Republic\n\nFacts:\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was born on 25 September 1868 in Chudenice in the Kingdom of Bohemia.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was sometimes referred to in English literature as the Czech Kingdom.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil died on 10 January 1950 in Prague.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
